WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.409 --> 00:00:08.809
We're in a new "Golden Age of Television"…not
to mention a "Golden Age of Unexpected TV

00:00:08.809 --> 00:00:13.679
Deaths." With the dramatic uptick in the quality
of TV shows came a commitment to keeping audiences

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:19.060
guessing with as many surprises as possible.
That means almost no character is safe. Here

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:23.050
are some deaths from the first half of 2016
that threw us for a loop. It should go without

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:25.279
saying, but...spoilers ahead.

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:27.510
Ziva David - NCIS

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:32.369
Former Mossad officer and NCIS agent Ziva
David, portrayed by Cote de Pablo, was one

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:36.960
of the most beloved characters on the most-watched
drama on TV. And when De Pablo left the show

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.200
to pursue new roles in 2014, her character's
story was wrapped up with a nice sendoff.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:46.670
So there really wasn't much need for Ziva
to ever be mentioned on NCIS again, which

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:51.579
is why it felt particularly cruel when it
was announced that the character had died—offscreen!—in

00:00:51.579 --> 00:00:54.299
a missile attack on her family home.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:56.840
"Vance got a call."

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.700
"Ziva…"

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.210
Denise - The Walking Dead

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:09.630
Emmy-winner Merritt Wever really had a nice
arc going as Denise on The Walking Dead. She

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:14.580
took over as town doctor in Alexandria after
her predecessor's untimely demise, she entered

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:19.000
into a romantic relationship with Tara despite
a fear of commitment, and she even survived

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:24.380
a hostage situation. She outlined her reasons
for diving into love with an impassioned monologue

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:30.050
on a supply run with Daryl and Rosita, explaining
she finally felt ready to stand up and fight

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:35.140
for her life. Only to be cut off by an arrow
through her eye and brain, shot from the woods

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.440
by a lurking Dwight.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:42.660
"Makes me sick, that you guys aren't even
trying. Because you're strong and you're smart.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:51.929
And you're both really good people. And if
you don't wake—up—and face your..."

00:01:51.929 --> 00:01:54.090
Robin Hood - Once Upon a Time

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:59.869
The long-running ABC show that has deftly
thrown together fairy tale icons, mythological

00:01:59.869 --> 00:02:05.050
characters, and Disney favorites only got
darker and more complicated in its fifth season.

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:09.340
Especially for Robin Hood, who just could
never catch a break. First, he found out his

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:14.280
beloved Maid Marian was actually Zelena, the
Wicked Witch of the West. And then Hades threatened

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:19.440
the life of his other true love, Regina, forcing
Robin to sacrifice himself to save her.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:20.960
"Sorry, ladies first."

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:22.140
"No!"

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:30.650
Ramsay Bolton - Game of Thrones

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:36.730
Murderer, sadist and serial rapist Ramsay
Bolton was arguably the most evil character

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:41.060
in the entire run of Game of Thrones. Which
is saying something on the show that gave

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:49.060
us Joffrey Baratheon. And since bad people
thrive on Game of Thrones, we expected him

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:54.590
to outlive...everyone. But after Ramsey goaded
Jon Snow into war, their conflict erupted

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:59.600
into the bloody "Battle of the Bastards."
Finally face-to-face with Jon, Ramsay tried

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:04.650
to avoid a physical fight by firing arrows
at him—only to be tackled, beaten bloody,

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:09.430
and tossed into a dungeon, where he suffered
the final indignity of being eaten alive by

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:14.290
his own dogs on the order of the wife he once
gleefully tortured.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.110
Hodor - Game of Thrones

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:22.430
Fans finally learned how Bran Stark's protector,
Hodor, got his name.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.651
"Hodor? Hodor!"

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:29.260
But it came in one of the most heartbreaking
plot twists in the show's history. Turns out

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:34.080
his name was really Wylis—but in a time-travel
mishap, Bran inadvertently showed young Wylis

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:38.790
a vision of his own death while serving as
a human barricade against a horde of zombies.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:43.700
The poor kid collapsed screaming "hold the
door," while in the present day, Hodor made

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:44.840
the ultimate sacrifice.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:51.250
"Hold the door! Hold the door! Hold the door!
Hold the door!"

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.790
We're really gonna miss you, big guy.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.770
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:02.260
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know which character deaths shocked you

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.090
the most this year…

